## 1. The window-update trigger path

### `tcp_should_send_recvwindow()` — nuttx/net/tcp/tcp_recvwindow.c:240-311

```c
  rcvseq = tcp_getsequence(conn->rcvseq);
  if (TCP_SEQ_GT(conn->rcv_adv, rcvseq))
    {
      oldwin = TCP_SEQ_SUB(conn->rcv_adv, rcvseq);
    }
  else
    {
      oldwin = 0;
    }

  win = tcp_get_recvwindow(dev, conn);

  /* If the window doesn't extend, don't send. */

  if (win <= oldwin)
    {
      ... return false;
    }

  adv = win - oldwin;

  maxwin = tcp_maxrcvwin(conn);
  if (2 * adv >= maxwin)   { return true; }

  mss = tcp_rx_mss(dev);
  if (adv >= 2 * mss)      { return true; }

  return false;
```

So: **true** iff `win > oldwin` AND (`2*adv >= maxwin` OR `adv >= 2*mss`). Note `oldwin` is derived *entirely* from `conn->rcv_adv` — the stack's belief about what it last advertised. There is no "was it actually transmitted" tracking.

